cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reproducibility artifacts, please cite it as below."
# 身份统一（审阅意见 2.1，2026-09-22）：本 artifact 的研究主线统一为「适应性学习中难度的
# 可测量化与可治理化」。学习成瘾指数（LAI）降级为**附属且未经验证**的模块，
# 不再出现在标题/摘要/关键词中，也不再作为本 artifact 的测量贡献声明。
type: software
title: "LearnFlow: A K12 Gamified Adaptive Learning Platform and Reproducibility Artifact for Difficulty Measurement, Calibration and Governance Research"
abstract: >-
  LearnFlow is a K12 gamified adaptive-learning platform released primarily as a reproducible
  research artifact for the study of difficulty in adaptive learning. The artifact supports four
  connected lines of work: (1) measurement — whether difficulty sources defined on different
  scales are commensurable, and how far a linear min-max fusion drifts under monotone
  reparameterisation relative to an empirical-CDF-to-logit quantile metric; (2) target — the
  external validity of the 80-85% success-rate rule on real learner logs; (3) decision —
  ordered difficulty sequencing under a cold start, including the reliability boundary of
  LLM-based difficulty annotation; (4) governance — an intervention ledger and a seven-tuple
  audit schema for the dozens of gamification mechanisms that coexist in one system.
  Every headline count in the documentation is recomputed from source by scripts under
  learnflow-backend/scripts/, and the consistency check fails loudly when a documented number
  diverges from the code.   The headline mechanism count is always reported as a triple —
  registered 54 / runtime effect producers 16 / maturity complete 9, partial 37, placeholder 8 —
  so the registered figure is never read as "54 mechanisms are running".
  The repository also contains a behavioural-log plus self-report measurement layer (a
  five-dimension learning-addiction index, LAI). It is an AUXILIARY, UNVALIDATED module: it has
  no user data, its self-report items are purpose-built and have not undergone psychometric
  validation, and it is not used or validated in any of the four lines of work above. It is
  retained for engineering completeness only, and the README states this limitation
  unconditionally.
